zeus@ccwf.cc.utexas.edu (Mark Gansle) writes:

>1) How do you convert an altar?

Offer a high-level monster to you god in an non-aligned altar.  There
is a good chance of succeeding if you yourself are a high-level
character.  Failure decreases your luck, and sometimes, a demon is
summoned to deal with you.

>2) Can you pray only at your god's altar, or any co-aligned altar?

Huh?  The only co-aligned altars belong to your god (unless you change
alignment).

If you pray at a non-aligned altar, you might be converted.

>3) What are the possible effects of #offering?

1. Blessing potions of water.
2. Getting a named weapon.
3. Improving your luck (you see a four-leaf clover).
4. Getting spellbooks.
5. Blessing / uncursing items.

This list is not exhaustive.

>4) Is there a way to figure out exactly what sort of monster corpse is
>going to make the Deity happy and what's going to be ignored (based on
>time, your level, dungeon level, and monster level)?

My rule of thumb: the nastier the monster, the more worthwhile your
offering.

